> 
> I am working with a pet purple worm at the (burrp!, excuse me) moment
> and quickly realized that there is not much loot left over.  Sure
> enough! digestion attacks don't leave corpses.  Do digestion attacks
> ever leave items remaining (I presume at least the Invocation items
> and the amulet)?

Yes. Everything but the corpse will be left behind. You can happily
let your purple worm chew up shopkeepers, priestesses etc. without
losing their loot.

With hostile purple worms, i _love_ to lure them to a watery death by
levitating over water adjacent to them. I've only recently done this
with a character wearing an amulet of magical breathing - not sure
whether that's required.

> Not that I'm complaining, but I'm only XL=9 so I'm very much looking
> to collect some treasure from the baddies.  I might have to leave him
> leashed up somewhere until I've done a quick pass through each level
> and relieved the denizens of their belongings.

Unnecessary.
In order to 'leash up' a purple worm (to keep it away from
monsters/NPCs you want to keep alive), just leave it behind a closed
door or a boulder.

